==English==

===Etymology===
Originally a medieval variant of {{term|Jack|lang=en}}, derived from {{term|John|lang=en}}; today also used as a diminutive form of {{term|Jacob|lang=en}} and {{term|James|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/d͡ʒeɪk/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪk}}

